Subject: [PATCH] Declare only the libc++ headers as LLVM compile inputs

On Bazel releases without the Merkle-tree input cache, the toolchain's
`include` filegroup feeds every compile action and globbed all of include/,
about 8,100 files of the LLVM distribution: the LLVM, Clang, MLIR, LLDB,
Flang, Polly and clang-tidy development headers as well as libc++. The
toolchain only puts include/c++/v1 and the per-target __config_site on the
search path, so the rest is never read; a remote executor still stages each of
those files for each action. Glob include/c++ instead, the same set the
directory-based `cxx_builtin_include` filegroup declares on newer Bazel.

diff --git a/toolchain/BUILD.llvm_repo.tpl b/toolchain/BUILD.llvm_repo.tpl
--- a/toolchain/BUILD.llvm_repo.tpl
+++ b/toolchain/BUILD.llvm_repo.tpl
@@ -56,7 +56,11 @@
 filegroup(
     name = "include",
     srcs = glob([
-        "include/**",
+        # Compiles search only the libc++ headers in include/c++ and the
+        # per-target __config_site (see extra_config_site). The LLVM, Clang,
+        # MLIR, LLDB and other development headers beside them are never on
+        # the search path, so they are not compile inputs.
+        "include/c++/**",
         "lib/clang/*/include/**",
     ]) + glob(
         [
